-- title:
--   Jacquet's lemma in polynomial recurrence form for GL₃
-- statement:
--   Let $v$ be a nonzero prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, write $\mathbb{Q}_v$ for the $v$-adic completion, and let $W\colon \mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)\to\mathbb{C}$ be a function. Let $V$ denote `gl3CyclicSubspace W`, the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the right translates $g\mapsto W(gh)$, $h\in\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)$. Assume: (i) $W$ is right invariant under some open subgroup $U_v$, i.e. $W(gk)=W(g)$ for all $k\in U_v$ and all $g$; (ii) for every open subgroup $U_v$ there is a finite set $B$ of functions $\mathrm{GL}_3(\mathbb{Q}_v)\to\mathbb{C}$ such that every $F\in V$ satisfying $F(gk)=F(g)$ for all $k\in U_v$ lies in the $\mathbb{C}$-span of $B$. Let $\varpi$ be an element of the valuation ring of $\mathbb{Q}_v$ whose image in $\mathbb{Q}_v$ is nonzero of valuation $\exp(-1)$, and let $\Phi\in V$. Then two assertions hold. First, there is a nonzero $C\in\mathbb{C}[X]$ with $$\sum_{i=0}^{\deg C} C_i\,\bigl(g\mapsto \Phi(g\,t_1^{\,i})\bigr)\in \mathrm{span}_{\mathbb{C}}\{\,g\mapsto G(g\,n)-G(g)\ :\ G\in V,\ n=\begin{pmatrix}1&w_0&w_1\\0&1&0\\0&0&1\end{pmatrix},\ w\in\mathbb{Q}_v^2\,\},$$ where $t_1=\mathrm{diag}(\varpi,1,1)$ is the image under the $2\times 2$ block embedding $\iota$ of $\mathrm{diag}(\varpi,1)$. Second, there is a nonzero $C\in\mathbb{C}[X]$ with the same conclusion for $t_2=\iota(\varpi\cdot 1_2)=\mathrm{diag}(\varpi,\varpi,1)$ and for the span of the differences $g\mapsto G(g\,n')-G(g)$ with $G\in V$ and $n'$ the unipotent matrix with first two entries $w_0,w_1$ in the last column.
--
--   This is Jacquet's lemma in recurrence form for the two maximal standard parabolic subgroups of $\mathrm{GL}_3$: modulo the subspace generated by differences along the unipotent radical, the translation operator by the central element of the Levi is annihilated by a nonzero polynomial. It is used in the local analysis of the cubic induction, feeding the evaluation of Rankin–Selberg local integrals and the finiteness of torus shell averages for $\mathrm{GL}_3$ Whittaker functions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_LanglandsTunnell_CubicInduction_exists_polynomial_sum_coeff_smul_rightTranslate_pow_mem_span_radical_of_admissible.lean

